From: dagu <dagu@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] device: Start LE GATT client after bonding completes

When bluetoothd initiates LE bonding (Device1.Pair), the ATT channel is
accepted at Pairing Request time and gatt_client_init() raises its
security to medium. The kernel releases the queued Exchange MTU Request
on Encryption Change, which is before SMP key distribution. A BT5.0 HID
mouse (23:15:1D:17:xx:xx) acks that PDU at the link layer, sends its
Encryption Information and Central Identification, and never answers
the ATT request. The client then sits on the 30 s ATT timeout, Pair
returns after the D-Bus timeout, and HoG only starts on a later
reconnect. On reconnect (no key distribution) the same mouse answers
Exchange MTU in 50 ms.

Hold the GATT client while our own LE bonding is in progress and start
it from device_bonding_complete(), so the first ATT request follows key
distribution, the same order Android uses (bond, then GATT discovery).
---
--- a/src/device.c
+++ b/src/device.c
@@ -210,6 +210,7 @@
 	struct btd_bearer *bredr;
 	struct btd_bearer *le;
 	bool		pending_paired;		/* "Paired" waiting for SDP */
+	bool		gatt_client_deferred;	/* waiting for LE bonding */
 	bool		svc_refreshed;
 	bool		refresh_discovery;
 
@@ -6051,6 +6052,8 @@
 
 	DBG("");
 
+	device->gatt_client_deferred = false;
+
 	if (device->browse)
 		goto done;
 
@@ -6357,7 +6360,22 @@
 		load_gatt_db(dev, btd_adapter_get_storage_dir(dev->adapter),
 								dstaddr);
 
-	gatt_client_init(dev);
+	/*
+	 * While our own LE bonding is in progress the link becomes encrypted
+	 * before SMP key distribution has finished, and the kernel releases
+	 * queued ATT at that point. Some HID peripherals drop an ATT request
+	 * that arrives while they are distributing keys and never answer it,
+	 * so Exchange MTU waits for the 30 s ATT timeout. Start the client
+	 * once bonding has completed instead.
+	 */
+	if (dev->bonding && dev->bonding->bdaddr_type != BDADDR_BREDR &&
+					sec_level < BT_IO_SEC_MEDIUM) {
+		DBG("Deferring GATT client until bonding completes");
+		gatt_client_cleanup(dev);
+		dev->gatt_client_deferred = true;
+	} else {
+		gatt_client_init(dev);
+	}
 	gatt_server_init(dev, database);
 
 	/*
@@ -7098,6 +7116,13 @@
 
 	DBG("bonding %p status 0x%02x", bonding, status);
 
+	/* Key distribution is over, success or not. */
+	if (device->gatt_client_deferred) {
+		device->gatt_client_deferred = false;
+		if (device->att)
+			gatt_client_init(device);
+	}
+
 	device->bonding_status = status;
 	if (status == MGMT_STATUS_AUTH_FAILED)
 		device_request_disconnect(device, NULL);
